   ("p", "This is the part that silently ruins exports. CSV separates fields with a delimiter, usually a comma, and rows with line breaks. So what happens when a value itself contains a comma, a line break, or a quotation mark? Without care, a description like Hello, world would look like two separate fields and shift every column after it out of alignment. The rule that fixes this is simple and universal: any field containing the delimiter, a double quote or a line break must be wrapped in double quotes, and any double quote inside such a field must be doubled."),
