   ("p", "Resize an image by dragging a corner and it stays crisp; drag an edge and everyone in the photo suddenly looks stretched. The difference is aspect ratio, the single idea that decides whether a resized image looks right or wrong. It sounds technical but it is just the relationship between width and height, and once you understand it you can resize anything without distortion and read a ratio like 16:9 with confidence. This guide explains what a ratio is, how to keep it, and how it simplifies, with the free <a href=\"../tools/aspect-ratio-calculator.html\">Aspect Ratio Calculator</a> to check your numbers."),
