   ("p", "Why is 1920 by 1080 called 16:9 rather than 1920:1080? Because a ratio is simplified by dividing both numbers by their greatest common divisor, the largest number that divides both exactly. For 1920 and 1080 that divisor is 120: 1920 divided by 120 is 16, and 1080 divided by 120 is 9, giving 16:9. The simplified form is the smallest whole-number pair with the same shape, which is why it is the version people quote. The calculator shows both the simplified ratio and the decimal value (16 divided by 9 is about 1.778), and the decimal is handy when you want to compare two shapes at a glance."),
