   ("h2", "The overnight problem"),
   ("p", "Now the second trap: a shift that crosses midnight. Someone clocks in at 22:00 and out at 06:00. In minutes since midnight the start is 1320 and the end is 360, and 360 minus 1320 is minus 960, a nonsensical negative sixteen hours. The end time looks earlier than the start because it belongs to the next day. The fix is to recognise that and add a full day, 24 hours or 1440 minutes, to the end before subtracting: 360 plus 1440 is 1800, and 1800 minus 1320 is 480 minutes, which is the correct 8 hours. Ticking the overnight option does this addition for you so you never see the negative."),
   ("tool", "time-duration-calculator", "Time Duration Calculator", "Enter a start and end time to get the exact duration in hours and minutes, decimal hours and total minutes; tick overnight for shifts that cross midnight and subtract an unpaid break."),
