   ("p", "For paid hours, the raw span is often not the answer, because an unpaid break sits inside it. The clean way to handle this is to work out the total duration first, then subtract the break as a flat number of minutes at the end, rather than trying to juggle it inside the clock arithmetic. An 09:00 to 17:30 span is 510 minutes; subtract a 30-minute lunch and you have 480 minutes, or 8 hours exactly. Keeping the break as a separate final subtraction keeps the calculation simple and easy to check."),
