   ("p", "Payroll systems and invoices almost always want decimal hours, not hours and minutes, and this is where another common error appears. Eight hours and thirty minutes is 8.5 hours, not 8.30, because you convert the minutes to a fraction of an hour by dividing by 60. Thirty minutes is 30 divided by 60, which is 0.5; fifteen minutes is 0.25; twenty minutes is 0.333. Writing 8.30 on a timesheet quietly underpays by turning 30 minutes into a third of what it should be."),
   ("callout", "The decimal shortcut", "To convert minutes to a decimal, divide by 60: 15 is 0.25, 30 is 0.5, 45 is 0.75. The calculator shows hours-and-minutes, decimal hours and total minutes at once, so you never have to convert by hand for a timesheet."),
